# Rules to skip for specific paths in this crate.
# Format: RULE/name:path/glob — gitignore-style glob relative to crate root.
# Every entry requires a WHY: comment. No blanket category ignores.

# WHY: koinon provides the shared domain types (Frequency, SignalKind,
# Timestamp, Baseline, TamperLog, etc.) re-exported via lib.rs `pub use`
# and consumed across the workspace. Item-definition files (baseline.rs,
# frequency.rs, …) must expose `pub` for those re-exports to compile
# (Rust E0365). Methods on those re-exported types form part of the
# public API surface. The RUST/pub-visibility rule exempts lib.rs/mod.rs
# but does not follow `pub use` chains into the defining files; this
# scoped ignore bridges that gap.
RUST/pub-visibility:src/**
